---
title: Manifest
order: 20
summary: Write the Deployment and the Service as YAML and apply them.
---

A second way to solve the same task. Every `solution.<name>.md` next to
`config.yaml` is an extra solution; `astrona docs solutions` lists them in
`order`, and `astrona docs solution --name manifest` shows this one.

```sh
astrona shell [[.Name]]
kubectl apply -f - <<'YAML'
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: web
  namespace: shop
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: web}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: web}
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx:1.27-alpine
          ports: [{containerPort: 80}]
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: web
  namespace: shop
spec:
  selector: {app: web}
  ports: [{port: 80, targetPort: 80}]
YAML
kubectl -n shop get deploy,pods,svc
exit
astrona submit
```

The pod label `app=web` is what both the Service selector and the checks look for.
